course: dictionary
lesson: 1221
title: Bulb: a light or a plant part
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so look at the words around it. «Electricity only flows when it has a complete loop to go round, from the battery, through the bulb and back again.» Here a bulb is the glass part that gives out light, because it sits in a loop with a battery.
explain: The same word can name a plant part. In «Schrenk's tulip... flowers early in spring... then hides as a bulb», a bulb is the round part under the ground where the plant stores food and a new plant grows. Nothing in that sentence is glass or electric.
explain: Ask yourself which meaning fits. Swap your meaning into the sentence: a light bulb is switched on, but a tulip bulb is hidden in the soil. If your meaning does not fit, try the other one.
fact: A bulb is the glass part of a lamp that gives out light when electricity flows through it.
fact: A bulb is also the round underground part of some plants, like tulips, onions and daffodils.
fact: «If there is any gap, the flow stops and the bulb goes out.»
fact: «Push the switch on a torch and you close a gap in the loop, so the bulb lights.»
fact: A light-bulb moment means a sudden good idea.
exercise: «Push the switch on a torch and you close a gap in the loop, so the bulb lights.» In this sentence, what is a bulb? | Food stored in the soil | Round underground part of a plant | A kind of battery | *Glass part that gives out light
exercise: «Schrenk's tulip... then hides as a bulb.» What does bulb mean here? | A part of a circuit that stops the flow | *The round underground part of a plant, where a new plant grows | A light that flickers | A swollen part of a thermometer
exercise: Which phrase means a sudden good idea? | *A light-bulb moment | A plant bulb | An LED bulb | An energy-saving bulb
test: In «If there is any gap, the flow stops and the bulb goes out», what happens when there is a gap? | *The flow stops and the bulb goes out | The bulb gets brighter | The flower opens in spring | The bulb is planted in autumn
test: Why do gardeners plant bulbs in autumn? | To make the bulb glow | Because summer dries everything | So they can switch them off | *So the plant can flower in spring
exam: Ayesha has a torch bulb and a tulip bulb. Which difference do the lesson clues show? | Both are planted in autumn | Neither has any use | Both give out light | *The torch bulb gives out light, and the tulip bulb is a round underground part of a plant
